# Golden output fixtures are compared byte for byte against a program's stdout, so git must not
# rewrite their line endings on checkout. Without this, a Windows runner reads CRLF out of a file
# committed with LF and every golden test fails there and only there — which is exactly how spec
# 0049 first went red on CI.
crates/cli/tests/golden/** -text

# Font programs are embedded with `include_bytes!` and subset byte-exactly into the PDF. Git's
# binary detection already gets this right, but the cost of it being wrong once — a face silently
# corrupted on one platform's checkout — is far higher than the cost of saying so.
*.ttf -text
*.otf -text
